Fun DraStic for Leaf on MLP1
============================

Fun DraStic is by tenlevels. It is a frontend - menus, overlays, screen
layouts, themes and presentation - attached to the closed-source DraStic
emulator through an LD_PRELOAD SDL hook (lib/libfundrastic.so). The emulator
binary itself, bin/drastic64, is the same prebuilt aarch64 DraStic binary the
primary DraStic package ships, byte for byte. Game compatibility, accuracy and
speed are therefore identical between the two; what differs is the interface.

The default Nintendo DS emulator on Leaf is the separate DraStic package built
on Steward Fu's steward-fu/nds project. Fun DraStic is an alternate you can
select per game. They are different packages by different authors and neither
is a build of the other.

The hook is compiled from tenlevels' source, not lifted from a binary drop:

  Source:        @SOURCE_REPO@
  Source commit: @SOURCE_COMMIT@
  funhook.c:     @FUNHOOK_SHA256@
  Built hook:    @HOOK_SHA256@

Fun DraStic's own code is under the PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0
(licenses/). DraStic, its free BIOS and the databases are Exophase's
proprietary freeware and keep their own terms - see licenses/CREDITS.md,
which is tenlevels' own credits file.

BIOS
----
DraStic's own free replacement BIOS ships in system/ and covers most games.
The optional Nintendo dumps are never included; see system/BIOS-README.txt for
the filenames and where to put them.

Where things live
-----------------
State and configuration:
  .userdata/<platform>/fun-drastic
In-game saves, savestates and their previews:
  Saves/NDS, Saves/NDS/states and Saves/NDS/previews
Support log:
  .userdata/<platform>/logs/fun-drastic.log

Nothing is written into the release-managed emulator directory at runtime, so
an update replaces the package cleanly.

In-game saves are shared with the primary DraStic package. Fun DraStic keeps
them in Saves/NDS as .sram; the primary DraStic package keeps them in its own
state directory as .dsv. Same bytes, different name. The launcher mirrors the
launched game's save in before launch and out after exit, newest wins.
Configuration and savestates are not shared.

Saves and savestates are named after the ROM's whole name, the same name the
primary DraStic package uses. Fun DraStic used to cut that name to its first
28 bytes. The first time you start a game with a longer name, the launcher
copies the files saved under the shorter name to the whole name and leaves the
originals in place.

Support diagnostics
-------------------
These are for maintainers and are off by default:

  FUN_HOOK=0                 run drastic64 without the Fun DraStic frontend
  FUN_EVLOG=1                log input events and frame pacing
  FUN_FF_SPEED=2..8          fast-forward multiplier
  FUN_DRASTIC_SHARE_SAVES=0  keep .dsv saves out of the primary DraStic package
  FUN_DRASTIC_BIOS_REFRESH=1 re-copy user BIOS files over the runtime copies
